# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
.next

# next-on-pages build output. Cloudflare Pages regenerates this on its own runner
# via `npm run pages:build`, so a committed copy is 950+ generated files that are
# stale the moment anyone edits a page — and they bury every real diff. This was
# committed by accident in 21bc326 and removed from tracking on 26 Jul 2026.
.vercel

# Local miniflare state for `wrangler pages dev` / `wrangler d1 execute --local`.
# SQLite files holding a local copy of the blog, recreated on demand and meaningless
# on another machine. Not ignored until 1 Aug 2026 — the first `pages dev` run in this
# repo would have committed them into the ONLY PUBLIC repo.
.wrangler

dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.env
.env.*
.dev.vars

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Agent-readable markdown, generated from lab/posts/ by scripts/build-agent-markdown.mjs.
# Not committed because it is genuinely derived: `npx @cloudflare/next-on-pages` runs
# `npm run build`, which runs the generator, so Cloudflare regenerates these on every
# deploy — verified, not assumed. Committing them would create a second copy of the posts
# that can disagree with lab/posts/, which is the exact failure this repo has a blog post
# about. If the Pages build command ever stops going through `npm run build`, these stop
# being emitted and this decision has to be revisited.
/public/md/
/public/llms-full.txt

# llms.txt joined them on 10 Aug 2026, generated by scripts/build-llms-txt.mjs from
# lab/posts/ plus data/llms.config.json. It was hand-written and tracked until then, and
# the reason for the change is that it proved the point above: the fourth lab post had to
# be appended by hand four days after publication, and /blog was never listed at all.
# Edit data/llms.config.json, not this output.
/public/llms.txt

# Third-party editorial feedback on lab posts, kept on disk and out of the repo.
# This repo is public and a push to main deploys the live site, so an internal
# critique must never be one `git add -A` away from publication.
/analysis.md
